  "response_text": "The stack pool is a reserved section of memory that holds stack space for each thread. Since each thread needs its own private stack to store local variables and register values, the pool is divided so each thread gets a separate chunk. In future labs, we can expand our OS to support multiple threads by assigning a different stack from the pool to each one, and then switching between them using context switching.\\n",
